 "capsule": "The Southern Xiongnu were the faction of the Xiongnu confederation that submitted to Han China around 50–51 CE under Chanyu Bi (Huhanye II), after the Xiongnu split into northern and southern wings amid succession war and famine in 48 CE. Settled inside the Han frontier in the Ordos region as a client state under a Han-appointed Protectorate, the Southern Xiongnu supplied auxiliary cavalry for Han campaigns against their Northern Xiongnu kin. Their chanyus continued to rule from within Han territory until the office was progressively absorbed into Han frontier administration in the early 2nd century CE.",
